1
00:00:22,930 --> 00:00:28,013
4 CONTESTANTS LEFT.
4 DAYS AND 14 HOURS UNTIL THE GAME ENDS.

2
00:00:33,316 --> 00:00:38,623
"Since you continue to act like a fool,
I have prepared a new stage for you."

3
00:00:42,108 --> 00:00:43,899
A new stage?

4
00:00:44,941 --> 00:00:45,736
Why are you here?

5
00:00:47,024 --> 00:00:48,650
I've brought you a scoop.

6
00:00:49,483 --> 00:00:50,330
A scoop?

7
00:00:51,191 --> 00:00:51,723
That's right.

8
00:00:53,149 --> 00:00:55,108
That's him!

9
00:00:57,536 --> 00:00:59,244
Don't call the cops yet.

10
00:01:01,774 --> 00:01:04,316
Let's have a good, long chat.

11
00:01:17,066 --> 00:01:18,483
Your face is cut.

12
00:01:21,233 --> 00:01:25,649
Police brutality.
Another detective with a bad temper.

13
00:01:28,191 --> 00:01:29,774
What happened to him?

14
00:01:31,691 --> 00:01:32,941
Dunno.

15
00:01:42,149 --> 00:01:43,566
What about Saori?

16
00:01:45,024 --> 00:01:48,483
Why even ask?
Do you think you can save her?

17
00:01:48,608 --> 00:01:49,703
Look, you...!

18
00:01:50,608 --> 00:01:52,191
You gonna hit me too?

19
00:01:54,316 --> 00:01:56,483
The game continues.

20
00:01:58,688 --> 00:02:00,688
What's this new stage?

21
00:02:03,149 --> 00:02:06,691
I dunno, but we've only got one option...

22
00:02:07,233 --> 00:02:11,233
Find the mastermind and rescue everyone.

23
00:02:12,441 --> 00:02:13,858
That's right.

24
00:02:15,108 --> 00:02:17,636
What happened five years ago?

25
00:02:18,425 --> 00:02:20,209
What hospital were you at?

26
00:02:25,358 --> 00:02:25,990
This one.

27
00:02:26,063 --> 00:02:28,233
TOKYO GENERAL MEDICAL CENTER

28
00:02:28,490 --> 00:02:31,210
Tokyo General Medical Center...

29
00:02:33,894 --> 00:02:34,852
What about it?

30
00:02:35,865 --> 00:02:39,240
No, that's not the one I was thinking of.

31
00:02:40,073 --> 00:02:43,198
I thought it might be the hospital

32
00:02:43,448 --> 00:02:46,948
from a case I was involved in five years ago.

33
00:02:47,906 --> 00:02:49,156
I see.

34
00:02:51,573 --> 00:02:56,573
An exclusive interview with
a perpetrator of the kiDnap GAME...

35
00:02:57,448 --> 00:02:59,448
A true journalist, I see.

36
00:03:00,323 --> 00:03:02,615
It'll serve as evidence.

37
00:03:05,323 --> 00:03:10,656
Come on, I know you want the scoop.
To clear your reputation.

38
00:03:13,156 --> 00:03:18,448
You published fake news
and ruined your credibility as a journalist.

39
00:03:19,365 --> 00:03:23,198
Now's your chance to redeem yourself.

40
00:03:23,865 --> 00:03:27,073
Is that why you're working with Niide?

41
00:03:27,198 --> 00:03:30,531
Or is it your loyalty to Saori?

42
00:03:33,034 --> 00:03:36,992
I'm doing it to find the truth.
And to rescue Saori.

43
00:03:43,031 --> 00:03:43,865
Let's begin.

44
00:03:50,531 --> 00:03:53,365
You're behind the abduction of...

45
00:03:53,531 --> 00:03:58,823
"KiDnap GAME."
That's more sensational.

46
00:04:00,073 --> 00:04:02,281
Was the crime your idea?

47
00:04:05,823 --> 00:04:10,531
The game was planned
by a nobler, more compassionate person.

48
00:04:12,365 --> 00:04:16,781
So you're just a pawn, is that right?

49
00:04:20,698 --> 00:04:22,115
I'm ready.

50
00:04:30,740 --> 00:04:32,073
I'll be going.

51
00:04:39,865 --> 00:04:43,906
I'm following orders... of my own will.

52
00:04:47,698 --> 00:04:49,406
What's the "scoop"?

53
00:04:53,240 --> 00:04:54,323
This.

54
00:04:56,156 --> 00:05:00,865
Broadcast this at 3 PM.

55
00:05:10,990 --> 00:05:12,156
What's on it?

56
00:05:12,573 --> 00:05:14,448
You'll find out.

57
00:05:18,781 --> 00:05:20,698
Can I ask you a favor?

58
00:05:21,198 --> 00:05:22,156
What?

59
00:05:25,605 --> 00:05:29,143
Five years ago,
you and Christina were in Tokyo.

60
00:05:30,281 --> 00:05:33,823
Miguel from Manila also once worked in Tokyo.

61
00:05:34,769 --> 00:05:35,603
Tokyo?

62
00:05:35,860 --> 00:05:37,043
Yeah.

63
00:05:38,073 --> 00:05:39,740
Maybe Tokyo's the key.

64
00:05:54,573 --> 00:05:58,698
Can I speak to the lead investigator
of the kiDnap GAME?

65
00:05:59,115 --> 00:06:02,323
Me? I'm the perpetrator.

66
00:06:03,448 --> 00:06:04,656
It's the perp.

67
00:06:05,573 --> 00:06:07,115
Put them through.

68
00:06:11,781 --> 00:06:14,156
This is Samejima.

69
00:06:19,073 --> 00:06:21,073
You think we'll accept that?

70
00:06:21,406 --> 00:06:22,948
I'll say it again.

71
00:06:23,073 --> 00:06:29,073
Remove all travel restrictions
on Toshiro Niide and Han Kiju.

72
00:06:29,656 --> 00:06:31,323
Who are you?

73
00:06:31,698 --> 00:06:35,448
If you refuse, the hostages will die.

74
00:06:39,198 --> 00:06:42,281
I have something to offer in return.

75
00:06:42,990 --> 00:06:44,531
In return?

76
00:07:03,452 --> 00:07:04,151
Who are you?

77
00:07:08,098 --> 00:07:09,848
Why are you doing this?

78
00:07:09,973 --> 00:07:12,765
Anyone... please!

79
00:07:13,603 --> 00:07:14,936
Are there others here, too?

80
00:07:16,311 --> 00:07:17,890
Is there anyone there?

81
00:07:25,436 --> 00:07:27,645
Please help!

82
00:07:40,853 --> 00:07:41,670
Yes?

83
00:07:42,353 --> 00:07:45,270
That man you were looking for...
He's here.

84
00:07:46,770 --> 00:07:48,103
Are you sure?

85
00:07:48,978 --> 00:07:51,311
He's inviting you and Han Kiju

86
00:07:53,853 --> 00:07:55,811
to the next stage.

87
00:07:58,436 --> 00:07:59,978
He wants to meet us?

88
00:09:06,895 --> 00:09:09,401
KIDNAP GAME

89
00:09:15,020 --> 00:09:17,895
PM 01:32 JST
TOKYO

90
00:09:40,311 --> 00:09:41,395
Audio coming up.

91
00:09:41,811 --> 00:09:45,353
Bringing in the monitor. Check positions.

92
00:09:45,478 --> 00:09:46,478
To the right.

93
00:09:46,968 --> 00:09:48,051
-Okay.
-Thanks.

94
00:09:48,283 --> 00:09:50,396
-Be ready to go live.
-Okay.

95
00:09:50,811 --> 00:09:51,978
Live?

96
00:09:52,163 --> 00:09:54,538
If needed. We got the go-ahead.

97
00:09:54,743 --> 00:09:57,201
Cut it out. This isn't a show.

98
00:09:58,136 --> 00:10:02,776
The moment the man whose wife was taken
meets her kidnapper...

99
00:10:03,145 --> 00:10:07,710
Isn't it the media's duty to report that?

100
00:10:16,186 --> 00:10:20,311
That's why you're going places.
You get it.

101
00:10:21,311 --> 00:10:24,645
Remember the agreement.
Broadcast at 3 PM.

102
00:10:41,811 --> 00:10:46,511
Mr. Niide! It's almost time. Any comment?

103
00:10:46,617 --> 00:10:47,597
Let us through.

104
00:10:47,637 --> 00:10:49,751
How are you feeling?

105
00:10:49,804 --> 00:10:50,943
Let us through.

106
00:10:51,103 --> 00:10:53,353
Cut that out! Let them through!

107
00:10:53,544 --> 00:10:56,416
-Mr. Niide! Just one comment!
-Stop it!

108
00:10:56,555 --> 00:10:58,847
KIDNAP GAME
CONFRONTING THE KIDNAPPER

109
00:10:59,884 --> 00:11:01,593
Stay calm, Niide.

110
00:11:09,185 --> 00:11:10,164
They're here!

111
00:11:17,923 --> 00:11:22,863
Niide. Kiju.
So glad you could make it.

112
00:11:32,250 --> 00:11:32,922
Stop!

113
00:11:35,208 --> 00:11:38,292
One more step
and your wife could die.

114
00:11:40,583 --> 00:11:41,750
What is this?

115
00:11:43,537 --> 00:11:46,329
-Have a seat.
-I asked you a question!

116
00:11:48,787 --> 00:11:50,162
It's starting.

117
00:11:50,476 --> 00:11:52,129
-Are we rolling?
-Rolling.

118
00:11:53,600 --> 00:11:58,080
Ah yes, angry as ever.
Is raging all you can do?

119
00:11:59,757 --> 00:12:02,632
No wonder the bodies are piling up.

120
00:12:03,798 --> 00:12:05,090
You killed them.

121
00:12:05,215 --> 00:12:09,548
Calm down or you'll lose
the chance I'm giving you.

122
00:12:10,048 --> 00:12:11,223
Chance?

123
00:12:12,296 --> 00:12:13,303
What do you mean?

124
00:12:14,257 --> 00:12:19,757
I will give a chance to you slaves of desire.

125
00:12:20,423 --> 00:12:23,173
That's why I've invited you here.

126
00:12:30,007 --> 00:12:33,965
If you can answer my question,
the game will end.

127
00:12:34,965 --> 00:12:38,798
The hostages might even be freed.

128
00:12:39,298 --> 00:12:41,173
Cut the bullshit!

129
00:12:41,965 --> 00:12:44,548
What's your goal?
Why target us?

130
00:12:44,897 --> 00:12:47,981
That's exactly what I was going to ask.

131
00:12:48,757 --> 00:12:51,965
Why were you chosen?

132
00:12:52,090 --> 00:12:55,673
Figure that out within the time limit
and you win.

133
00:12:57,215 --> 00:13:01,632
You might even save
your beloved wife and daughter.

134
00:13:01,798 --> 00:13:04,423
-Saori better be safe...
-Hey, hey!

135
00:13:09,257 --> 00:13:10,882
What you're saying...

136
00:13:12,007 --> 00:13:18,465
is if we figure out why we were chosen,
the game ends and the hostages are released.

137
00:13:20,090 --> 00:13:24,382
Very good, my dear rational super-doctor!

138
00:13:25,632 --> 00:13:29,090
You're buying time while you think.

139
00:13:29,215 --> 00:13:34,132
At the same time, you're confirming
whether I can speak Korean.

140
00:13:34,988 --> 00:13:37,449
So unlike the sinner who only rages.

141
00:13:40,110 --> 00:13:43,371
Is the reason related to Tokyo?

142
00:13:45,424 --> 00:13:48,630
You'll have to be more specific.

143
00:13:51,069 --> 00:13:55,096
By the way, you only get one answer.
And the time limit is...

144
00:13:56,857 --> 00:13:59,263
Let's see... Five minutes.

145
00:14:00,027 --> 00:14:02,023
Well then... Go ahead.

146
00:14:06,697 --> 00:14:10,031
Are you gonna listen to this guy, Kiju?

147
00:14:10,406 --> 00:14:11,656
Niide.

148
00:14:16,156 --> 00:14:17,169
Do you need space?

149
00:14:18,197 --> 00:14:22,295
Um... Feel free to use this space
up to this line.

150
00:14:23,572 --> 00:14:24,705
Five minutes.

151
00:14:36,364 --> 00:14:39,850
-Seven participants.
-Yeah.

152
00:14:41,156 --> 00:14:46,947
Nationality, age, work... Everything differs.
But something must connect us.

153
00:14:47,531 --> 00:14:49,406
That's why we were chosen.

154
00:14:53,031 --> 00:14:53,947
And...?

155
00:15:03,531 --> 00:15:09,447
You called us "slaves of desire" just now.

156
00:15:09,572 --> 00:15:14,906
I will give a chance to you slaves of desire.

157
00:15:17,031 --> 00:15:18,697
You said it before, too.

158
00:15:18,875 --> 00:15:23,334
Why did you choose us?
What are you trying to achieve?

159
00:15:23,989 --> 00:15:27,781
So nosy. Insatiable.

160
00:15:29,174 --> 00:15:30,841
You're slaves to desire.

161
00:15:32,006 --> 00:15:33,589
Why "desire"?

162
00:15:36,281 --> 00:15:40,989
"Desire"... Humans have various desires...

163
00:15:42,822 --> 00:15:44,322
Besides that...

164
00:15:45,114 --> 00:15:50,531
You often criticize my character.

165
00:15:50,656 --> 00:15:55,239
The fact that you're here
means that you destroyed our dummy.

166
00:15:55,783 --> 00:15:56,866
So predictable.

167
00:15:57,200 --> 00:16:01,643
Ah yes, angry as ever.
Is raging all you can do?

168
00:16:03,450 --> 00:16:06,033
He used the word "sinner," too.

169
00:16:06,190 --> 00:16:08,399
So unlike the sinner who only rages.

170
00:16:17,972 --> 00:16:19,222
A red rose...

171
00:16:23,337 --> 00:16:27,379
There are red rose petals
at every crime scene.

172
00:16:28,254 --> 00:16:33,296
And with each body.
But the number of petals is different.

173
00:16:35,879 --> 00:16:40,156
-I had five... You had four...
-That's right.

174
00:16:41,048 --> 00:16:45,649
Each had a different number,
from one to seven.

175
00:16:47,337 --> 00:16:48,754
Seven people...

176
00:16:54,728 --> 00:16:56,853
The seven deadly sins...

177
00:16:58,587 --> 00:17:00,212
The seven deadly sins.

178
00:17:01,671 --> 00:17:07,129
Wrath, greed, lust,

179
00:17:09,004 --> 00:17:13,837
sloth, pride, gluttony,

180
00:17:13,962 --> 00:17:16,630
and envy.

181
00:17:19,173 --> 00:17:23,230
Wrath, greed, lust, sloth,

182
00:17:23,978 --> 00:17:28,123
pride, gluttony, and envy...
Those seven.

183
00:17:30,553 --> 00:17:33,603
They're all desires, in a sense.

184
00:17:34,845 --> 00:17:37,220
Does one match each player?

185
00:17:41,712 --> 00:17:42,921
Manila.

186
00:17:45,633 --> 00:17:48,341
I heard he is obsessed with money.

187
00:17:50,296 --> 00:17:51,796
He must be "greed."

188
00:17:52,671 --> 00:17:54,212
GREED
MANILA

189
00:17:54,921 --> 00:17:59,837
Christina's adultery must fall under "lust."

190
00:17:59,962 --> 00:18:00,837
LUST
TAIPEI

191
00:18:01,796 --> 00:18:02,712
And Bangkok?

192
00:18:04,380 --> 00:18:08,116
Apparently, she used to be dependent
on marijuana.

193
00:18:08,837 --> 00:18:11,004
That's "gluttony."

194
00:18:11,129 --> 00:18:13,504
GLUTTONY
BANGKOK

195
00:18:14,296 --> 00:18:17,829
"Sloth" must be
the cabin attendant in Singapore.

196
00:18:18,337 --> 00:18:20,337
SLOTH
SINGAPORE

197
00:18:20,978 --> 00:18:22,311
Always late.

198
00:18:22,612 --> 00:18:25,503
She was even late
the night of the kidnapping.

199
00:18:25,598 --> 00:18:27,616
SORRY, I'LL BE A BIT LATE...

200
00:18:28,296 --> 00:18:31,421
My sin must be... "wrath"...

201
00:18:31,587 --> 00:18:34,070
WRATH
TOKYO

202
00:18:34,887 --> 00:18:40,220
That leaves "pride" and "envy."
Which fits you?

203
00:18:41,422 --> 00:18:43,172
I don't envy anyone.

204
00:18:44,468 --> 00:18:46,389
You don't strike me as prideful.

205
00:18:47,630 --> 00:18:53,337
If anything, that fat-cat software engineer
in Naha's the proud one.

206
00:18:54,629 --> 00:18:59,004
Some might think
I avoid surgery out of pride...

207
00:18:59,296 --> 00:19:01,212
I don't think that's it.

208
00:19:10,629 --> 00:19:11,671
No time.

209
00:19:12,141 --> 00:19:16,995
And... It's time.

210
00:19:17,234 --> 00:19:21,110
What's your answer?

211
00:19:31,732 --> 00:19:35,723
We all committed different sins.

212
00:19:38,315 --> 00:19:41,982
And that's why you chose us.

213
00:19:44,774 --> 00:19:51,315
Wrath, greed, lust, sloth,

214
00:19:51,857 --> 00:19:55,399
pride, gluttony, and envy.

215
00:19:57,524 --> 00:20:02,107
We committed the seven deadly sins.

216
00:20:03,815 --> 00:20:08,530
That's why you targeted us
and made us play this game.

217
00:20:32,399 --> 00:20:33,774
Too bad. Incorrect.

218
00:20:36,149 --> 00:20:39,149
-Wait.
-I said you get one try.

219
00:20:39,274 --> 00:20:43,524
What a waste.
You squandered your one chance.

220
00:20:44,690 --> 00:20:46,524
Your daughter...

221
00:20:47,440 --> 00:20:52,607
and your wife
must be very disappointed in you.

222
00:20:58,440 --> 00:21:02,732
Answer me. Where is Saori?
I said where!

223
00:21:03,065 --> 00:21:04,440
-Niide.
-Let go!

224
00:21:06,607 --> 00:21:11,107
If you don't answer,
I'll kill you right here.

225
00:21:15,149 --> 00:21:19,940
That's it. This is your sin.

226
00:21:23,649 --> 00:21:26,274
You let your rage take over

227
00:21:26,502 --> 00:21:30,252
and become blind to everything around you.

228
00:21:33,050 --> 00:21:36,217
You haven't changed at all.

229
00:21:49,550 --> 00:21:53,800
Put your anger aside.
Show your kindness...

230
00:21:54,300 --> 00:21:58,842
Kindness that shields the weak...

231
00:21:59,675 --> 00:22:04,988
That's the right thing to do.

232
00:22:18,425 --> 00:22:22,259
Because of you, your wife...
Poor thing...

233
00:22:28,950 --> 00:22:30,491
Stop it, Niide!

234
00:22:32,425 --> 00:22:34,730
-Niide! Stop!
-Get off me!

235
00:22:35,543 --> 00:22:38,768
-Niide! Niide!
-Calm down!

236
00:22:38,793 --> 00:22:40,896
-Get off!
-Niide!

237
00:22:43,069 --> 00:22:45,610
Beating him up won't help.

238
00:23:00,300 --> 00:23:03,009
Do you know what a red rose means?

239
00:23:06,425 --> 00:23:10,259
"You are the only one. I love you."

240
00:23:14,675 --> 00:23:18,342
And what about a black rose?

241
00:23:29,259 --> 00:23:32,925
How apt to call this a theatrical crime.

242
00:23:33,550 --> 00:23:39,009
All the props are in their places,
all the actors in their roles.

243
00:23:40,231 --> 00:23:43,795
I'm playing my role till the end.

244
00:23:48,110 --> 00:23:52,550
And what is that? What's your role?

245
00:23:54,009 --> 00:23:58,092
To hand over the footage
containing the big scoop.

246
00:24:04,717 --> 00:24:05,967
It's time.

247
00:24:14,800 --> 00:24:18,800
This will be shown simultaneously
around the world.

248
00:24:28,390 --> 00:24:31,973
Five... four... three...

249
00:24:32,711 --> 00:24:33,503
two...

250
00:24:34,128 --> 00:24:35,253
one...

251
00:24:35,669 --> 00:24:36,383
zero.

252
00:24:36,711 --> 00:24:37,878
Switch the feed!

253
00:24:38,586 --> 00:24:44,616
Breaking news! A wave of simultaneous
kidnappings has struck seven cities in Asia!

254
00:24:45,130 --> 00:24:48,320
We have what appears to be the manifesto

255
00:24:48,452 --> 00:24:50,661
of the chief perpetrator.

256
00:24:51,040 --> 00:24:52,753
The manifesto?

257
00:25:08,779 --> 00:25:13,529
Humans are beings who feel anguish
and endure it.

258
00:25:14,196 --> 00:25:20,404
Yet you... you live free of anguish,
ignorant of your mistakes.

259
00:25:21,404 --> 00:25:24,487
Guilt does not torment you.

260
00:25:24,612 --> 00:25:26,737
You are oblivious...

261
00:25:28,255 --> 00:25:30,171
It is unforgivable.

262
00:25:30,450 --> 00:25:33,317
But I have prepared a fitting penance.

263
00:25:34,889 --> 00:25:41,843
If you wish to atone,
bring your honor, wealth, prospects, life...

264
00:25:42,645 --> 00:25:44,937
and stake them all.

265
00:25:46,100 --> 00:25:50,149
I have taken your dearest,
most beloved person from you.

266
00:25:51,065 --> 00:25:55,316
So how far will you go...
to get that person back?

267
00:25:56,865 --> 00:25:58,436
What is the kiDnap GAME?

268
00:25:59,413 --> 00:26:01,955
It’s a game of crime and punishment.

269
00:26:02,237 --> 00:26:06,737
It forces you to see and face
your sins of heedless evil,

270
00:26:07,654 --> 00:26:11,946
compels you to choose,
demands a bitter decision.

271
00:26:13,279 --> 00:26:16,696
Humans, who have that spiritual brake
called reason,

272
00:26:17,112 --> 00:26:20,154
are able to control themselves
in daily life.

273
00:26:20,555 --> 00:26:24,221
Yet when something dearer than their own lives
is at risk,

274
00:26:24,487 --> 00:26:26,987
they never think to apply that brake.

275
00:26:27,612 --> 00:26:32,404
Rushing forward, they sacrifice everything,
even themselves,

276
00:26:32,946 --> 00:26:36,029
in a cascading rampage of madness.

277
00:26:37,904 --> 00:26:40,696
All humans dwell in a sea of options.

278
00:26:40,946 --> 00:26:44,321
Your own decisions are no stranger to folly.

279
00:26:44,571 --> 00:26:48,654
The results of these people’s choices
will illustrate this.

280
00:26:48,821 --> 00:26:52,446
How foolish will people become
for the ones they love?

281
00:26:52,779 --> 00:26:56,737
By the end of the game,
the answer will be clear.

282
00:27:19,362 --> 00:27:22,362
Each player has committed a grave sin.

283
00:27:23,154 --> 00:27:26,529
They might assume
I mean the seven deadly sins.

284
00:27:26,654 --> 00:27:28,529
But that is wrong.

285
00:27:33,237 --> 00:27:37,612
The players are blindly evil.
Utterly guilty.

286
00:27:40,946 --> 00:27:42,904
They indulged...

287
00:27:48,446 --> 00:27:51,404
in the eight evil thoughts.

288
00:27:53,529 --> 00:27:55,862
"Eight evil thoughts"?

289
00:27:59,237 --> 00:28:05,737
They're the progenitors of the seven sins,
though slightly different.

290
00:28:14,696 --> 00:28:16,237
The number of petals.

291
00:28:17,029 --> 00:28:18,237
What about them?

292
00:28:18,946 --> 00:28:21,571
The number is different each time.

293
00:28:23,904 --> 00:28:28,696
They match the weight of each sin
of the eight evil thoughts.

294
00:28:30,279 --> 00:28:31,321
EVIL THOUGHTS

295
00:28:31,572 --> 00:28:33,585
Evil thoughts...?

296
00:28:35,718 --> 00:28:38,710
But what are the eight evil thoughts?

297
00:28:39,710 --> 00:28:42,654
Our ignorant players shall illustrate.

298
00:28:46,523 --> 00:28:50,882
Gluttony: a woman far too hungry for drugs.

299
00:28:59,737 --> 00:29:03,612
Hey, next time, text me if you want.

300
00:29:03,737 --> 00:29:06,696
I will give you a good price.

301
00:29:07,112 --> 00:29:10,862
MAKE BENZ WANG ADMIT AND PUBLICLY
CONFESS HIS DRUG SYNDICATE TIES.

302
00:29:11,404 --> 00:29:14,987
Lust: an adulterous model.

303
00:29:19,987 --> 00:29:21,737
You're not filming again are you?

304
00:29:22,404 --> 00:29:24,904
No! And I deleted the old video.

305
00:29:25,071 --> 00:29:28,237
EXPOSE THE SEX VIDEO WITH YOUR
AFFAIR PARTNER TO THE LIGHT OF DAY

306
00:29:28,946 --> 00:29:33,529
Greed: a taxi driver addicted to money.

307
00:29:41,301 --> 00:29:44,176
You conned that money
from those tourists, didn’t you?

308
00:29:45,294 --> 00:29:47,544
Life isn’t all about money.

309
00:29:47,821 --> 00:29:50,696
PREPARE 10 MILLION PESOS IN CASH.

310
00:29:51,218 --> 00:29:56,585
Wrath: a police detective who rages
in the name of justice.

311
00:30:03,685 --> 00:30:04,976
Where is she?!

312
00:30:07,020 --> 00:30:08,520
Stop it, Niide!

313
00:30:14,231 --> 00:30:18,939
Despair: a doctor who ignores
lives he could save.

314
00:30:22,389 --> 00:30:23,557
Despair?

315
00:30:29,383 --> 00:30:31,660
Will she go blind?

316
00:30:32,577 --> 00:30:34,183
You said it would succeed...

317
00:30:36,077 --> 00:30:38,104
That you'd fix her eyes...

318
00:30:48,302 --> 00:30:52,718
Sloth: a flight attendant
who’s never on time.

319
00:30:55,225 --> 00:30:56,767
Sloth?!

320
00:31:05,850 --> 00:31:09,309
-Sorry, the traffic was so bad!
-Sit down.

321
00:31:09,434 --> 00:31:13,309
CLEAR THE CHECKPOINTS WITHIN
THE TIME LIMITS AND REACH THE GOAL.

322
00:31:14,100 --> 00:31:20,170
Vanity: an upstart software engineer
with a career built on lies.

323
00:31:21,298 --> 00:31:22,349
"Upstart"...?

324
00:31:23,250 --> 00:31:24,750
How dare you!

325
00:31:29,350 --> 00:31:32,267
You're here now! In my world!

326
00:31:32,850 --> 00:31:36,184
Do you understand that your son
is a world-famous CEO?

327
00:31:37,684 --> 00:31:42,684
-That's seven...
-Eight evil thoughts?

328
00:31:43,892 --> 00:31:45,023
There's one more.

329
00:31:52,309 --> 00:31:54,379
And finally, pride.

330
00:31:57,142 --> 00:31:58,475
Another player?

331
00:31:59,392 --> 00:32:00,600
Who?

332
00:32:04,350 --> 00:32:08,550
HONG KONG

333
00:32:15,225 --> 00:32:16,836
My client is innocent.

334
00:32:17,596 --> 00:32:22,475
There's ample evidence of corruption.
The odds are against you.

335
00:32:22,600 --> 00:32:27,850
I've always succeeded in spite of the odds.
This time is no different.

336
00:32:31,684 --> 00:32:34,267
Do you know about the kiDnap GAME?

337
00:32:37,775 --> 00:32:41,076
I've heard rumors. What of it?

338
00:32:41,684 --> 00:32:44,725
The perpetrator released a manifesto.

339
00:32:48,267 --> 00:32:51,600
A heavyweight international lawyer
in Hong Kong

340
00:32:51,934 --> 00:32:56,142
who wins his cases by any means necessary.

341
00:33:01,225 --> 00:33:06,309
Look at this old case, Andy.
Isn't it similar to this one?

342
00:33:08,267 --> 00:33:10,809
You're right, Sylvia.

343
00:33:12,225 --> 00:33:14,392
We can use this. Well done.

344
00:33:31,350 --> 00:33:33,142
FLOWER SHOP
ATRA

345
00:33:43,230 --> 00:33:45,467
This lawyer used his money and influence

346
00:33:45,492 --> 00:33:48,447
to suppress the news
of his sister’s abduction.

347
00:33:49,734 --> 00:33:52,693
A toast to Andy's latest victory!

348
00:33:53,517 --> 00:33:55,392
-Thanks.
-Cheers.

349
00:33:56,027 --> 00:33:57,027
Sorry.

350
00:34:03,767 --> 00:34:05,807
YOU HAVE BEEN ENLISTED IN THE
KIDNAP GAME.

351
00:34:08,609 --> 00:34:11,160
He left the investigation to the police...

352
00:34:15,950 --> 00:34:17,683
That's none of your business.

353
00:34:18,147 --> 00:34:23,647
Your job is to do everything in your power
to locate and rescue her!

354
00:34:24,023 --> 00:34:27,956
while working in the shadows
to complete his mission.

355
00:34:29,477 --> 00:34:32,144
Mr. Wong, isn't this about you?

356
00:34:32,269 --> 00:34:35,019
Didn't your sister just pass the bar?

357
00:34:35,394 --> 00:34:36,977
Was she kidnapped?

358
00:34:37,644 --> 00:34:39,102
Why keep it secret?

359
00:34:39,602 --> 00:34:41,091
What's this "mission"?

360
00:34:41,852 --> 00:34:44,644
This has nothing to do with me.

361
00:34:47,935 --> 00:34:51,310
Sir! Please wait!

362
00:34:52,894 --> 00:34:54,566
Why release a manifesto?!

363
00:34:57,473 --> 00:35:01,309
Eight evil thoughts.
Eight evil players.

364
00:35:01,977 --> 00:35:03,343
Five yet remain.

365
00:35:04,264 --> 00:35:09,209
Only one shall prevail...
the first to complete the assigned mission.

366
00:35:24,563 --> 00:35:26,336
Only one shall survive.

367
00:35:37,314 --> 00:35:40,814
The hell of my creation continues...

368
00:35:50,981 --> 00:35:55,214
Why? Why release a manifesto now?

369
00:35:56,314 --> 00:35:59,356
Don't you like being a global celebrity?

370
00:36:02,523 --> 00:36:04,606
Is that your goal?

371
00:36:06,648 --> 00:36:08,189
To corner us?

372
00:36:08,314 --> 00:36:10,564
Niide! That's enough!

373
00:36:15,023 --> 00:36:17,398
-We'd like to speak to...
-Okay.

374
00:36:18,023 --> 00:36:19,481
Excuse me.

375
00:36:37,773 --> 00:36:40,274
In exchange for removal of
your travel restrictions,

376
00:36:40,952 --> 00:36:43,827
he offered to turn himself in.

377
00:36:46,957 --> 00:36:50,665
I could easily detain you right now,

378
00:36:51,606 --> 00:36:54,189
but it would endanger the hostages.

379
00:36:56,174 --> 00:37:01,507
Niide... I need you to cooperate
as a police detective.

380
00:37:06,814 --> 00:37:10,646
-My mission is to capture the mastermind.
-Then you should...

381
00:37:10,731 --> 00:37:14,160
Without using the police.

382
00:37:15,679 --> 00:37:19,587
DO NOT NOTIFY OR REQUEST ASSISTANCE
FROM STATE AUSHORITIES.

383
00:37:23,721 --> 00:37:27,867
Don't forget
that you're an officer of the law.

384
00:37:44,814 --> 00:37:48,439
Promise me you won't broadcast any of this.

385
00:37:51,023 --> 00:37:53,229
Ethically, we can't air it.

386
00:37:56,439 --> 00:37:57,773
Pull it.

387
00:38:04,125 --> 00:38:05,059
Niide.

388
00:38:07,231 --> 00:38:09,689
I have to tell you something.

389
00:38:10,273 --> 00:38:12,398
I can't reach Hyodo.

390
00:38:14,481 --> 00:38:18,731
That man talked like he'd encountered him...

391
00:38:18,981 --> 00:38:21,523
-You don't think...
-Stop.

392
00:38:27,106 --> 00:38:28,398
Don't go there.

393
00:38:33,394 --> 00:38:37,185
Akina, I want you to drop this case.

394
00:38:38,227 --> 00:38:40,580
You might get hurt as well.

395
00:38:40,644 --> 00:38:43,700
-If that's what it takes...
-I'm the target.

396
00:38:47,644 --> 00:38:48,473
We're the targets.

397
00:38:59,394 --> 00:39:00,644
Goodbye.

398
00:39:06,560 --> 00:39:10,144
Can I ask you one last thing?

399
00:39:13,519 --> 00:39:15,852
What "sin" did you commit?

400
00:39:18,685 --> 00:39:21,227
It's "wrath," for sure...

401
00:39:23,810 --> 00:39:28,477
There have been several times
when my anger caused trouble.

402
00:39:31,810 --> 00:39:33,352
Five years ago, too.

403
00:39:43,560 --> 00:39:46,060
I chased a speeder in a rage.

404
00:40:28,977 --> 00:40:33,269
The student driving was high.
They took him to a hospital.

405
00:40:35,185 --> 00:40:36,935
But he didn't survive.

406
00:40:40,935 --> 00:40:47,894
You wanted to chase?
You wanted to kill him, didncha?

407
00:40:49,019 --> 00:40:50,840
Are you happy now?

408
00:40:51,121 --> 00:40:53,496
-It's your fault!
-You killed him!

409
00:40:54,288 --> 00:40:57,079
Why... why?

410
00:41:01,746 --> 00:41:06,121
That's why you transferred
to Community Safety?

411
00:41:07,204 --> 00:41:08,007
Yeah.

412
00:41:10,871 --> 00:41:16,704
At the time, all I felt was anger.

413
00:41:19,538 --> 00:41:22,371
Out of anger, I chased him...

414
00:41:24,621 --> 00:41:25,996
and killed him.

415
00:41:30,204 --> 00:41:31,954
It doesn't change.

416
00:41:35,246 --> 00:41:36,996
It's always the same.

417
00:41:39,288 --> 00:41:41,496
I can't control my anger.

418
00:41:46,163 --> 00:41:48,954
I can't do "what's right."

419
00:41:57,204 --> 00:42:04,704
Someone like me shouldn't be a detective...

420
00:42:08,621 --> 00:42:10,121
I'm not so sure.

421
00:42:13,788 --> 00:42:16,788
I think the Toshiro Niide I know

422
00:42:17,746 --> 00:42:20,663
needs to stay on as a detective.

423
00:42:23,496 --> 00:42:29,746
The Toshiro Niide who's kind to those
who are vulnerable can do what's right.

424
00:42:41,121 --> 00:42:45,788
Swear to me.
That you'll do what's right.

425
00:42:49,496 --> 00:42:53,829
Put your anger aside.
Show your kindness...

426
00:42:55,996 --> 00:43:00,496
Kindness that shields the weak...

427
00:43:02,788 --> 00:43:09,871
That's the right thing to do.

428
00:43:18,329 --> 00:43:19,579
You're right.

429
00:43:23,454 --> 00:43:28,371
I swore I'd never lose control
to anger ever again.

430
00:43:31,829 --> 00:43:36,954
Akina... We'll take it from here.
So you don't need to...

431
00:43:39,538 --> 00:43:43,038
If you say not to get involved, I won't.

432
00:43:43,288 --> 00:43:48,621
But I'll still continue pursuing the truth.

433
00:43:52,038 --> 00:43:53,204
Fine...

434
00:43:59,971 --> 00:44:05,627
You said that student
who died five years ago was high?

435
00:44:06,280 --> 00:44:09,133
Yeah, sky-high on illegal drugs.

436
00:44:11,907 --> 00:44:12,831
Marijuana?

437
00:44:14,153 --> 00:44:17,496
I can't tell without looking it up.

438
00:44:20,413 --> 00:44:22,996
But if so, the woman in Bangkok...

439
00:44:23,121 --> 00:44:26,788
Aum was a cannabis-addicted drug dealer.

440
00:44:27,913 --> 00:44:29,704
That might be a link.

441
00:44:40,329 --> 00:44:42,079
What's this about?

442
00:44:49,871 --> 00:44:51,454
Why do this?

443
00:44:58,927 --> 00:45:02,327
I HAVE A GIFT FOR MY PLAYERS.
VIDEO CONFERENCE IN ONE HOUR.

444
00:45:02,400 --> 00:45:04,953
PARTICIPATE OR BE DISQUALIFIED.

445
00:49:35,480 --> 00:49:36,280
I'm ready.

446
00:49:44,823 --> 00:49:45,536
I'll be going.

447
00:49:48,755 --> 00:49:49,736
Ah.

448
00:49:52,230 --> 00:49:53,855
A black rose...

449
00:49:55,564 --> 00:49:57,314
To me, it looks black.

450
00:49:59,355 --> 00:50:04,105
There are many meanings
attributed to a black rose.

451
00:50:08,345 --> 00:50:09,320
I wonder which one it is.
